From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:55:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvhttp: a client's quit ends its own stream, not
 everyone's

cancel stopped every session and unplugged every client's gamepads, whoever
asked: one guest leaving through Moonlight's Quit ended the game for all of
them. It stops the asking client's session only, as disabling that client
already does, and is the quit it was once no session is left.
---
 src/nvhttp.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvhttp.cpp b/src/nvhttp.cpp
index c234157..1040568 100644
--- a/src/nvhttp.cpp
+++ b/src/nvhttp.cpp
@@ -1601,6 +1601,13 @@ namespace nvhttp {
     tree.put("root.cancel", 1);
     tree.put("root.<xmlattr>.status_code", 200);
 
+    // Only this client's own stream and gamepads: others may still be playing.
+    rtsp_stream::terminate_sessions_by_cert(client_of(request).cert);
+
+    if (rtsp_stream::session_count() > 0) {
+      return;
+    }
+
     rtsp_stream::terminate_sessions();
 
     if (proc::proc.running() > 0) {
-- 
